led\n\n### **Purpose**\nThis function is specifically designed for **Dream-mode review** (used by Dream Review Director only). It persists review reports to `dream_reports/{dream_id}/{tier}/review_report.md` instead of the standard research-phase submission path. Key differences from the standard submission tool:\n- Writes only to Dream-specific directory structure\n- Does NOT send the report to Research Director\n- Dream Tool orchestrator reads the file once the subprocess exits\n- Skips the cross-round review protocol guards that apply to real submissions\n- Supports optional Group C visibility with a `[Dream]` prefix\n\n### **Tool Registry Status**\nThe function is registered in the MCP tool registry for the `dream_review_director` role in `/home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tool_registry.py` (line 477):\n```python\n_DREAM_REVIEW_DIRECTOR_TOOLS = frozenset({\n    \"director_post_to_reviewer\",\n    \"submit_dream_review_report\",  # ← Here\n    \"director_get_project_overview\",\n    \"read_local_file\",\n    \"read_project_file\",\n})\n```"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a809893-9edf-45cd-a05c-395ee786b54e","uuid":"4ef42225-0a1b-42d5-8f93-78104c502881","timestamp":"2026-05-11T23:47:52.907Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Search for \"submit_dream_review_report\" in the codebase. Look under /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/ for any Python file that defines or registers this function/tool. Also check if it might be a method name in an MCP server. Report the exact file path, function signature, and parameter names.","agentId":"a7b610cd9589f7228","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive report with all the findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found **`submit_dream_review_report`** defined in the codebase. Here are the details:\n\n### **Primary Location (Actual Implementation)**\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tools/feishu_group.py`  \n**Lines:** 1244-1351\n\n### **MC